[38;2;124;124;124mlevelwise $(\mathbb{S} \wedge X) \wedge \mathbb{S}^{\wedge n} \wedge M \simeq X [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\wedge M$, hence its colimit is $X \wedge M$) — we obtain:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$(\mathbb{S} \wedge X) \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} (\mathbb{S} \wedge Y) \simeq X [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\wedge (\mathbb{S} \wedge Y) \simeq X \wedge Y.$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore $F(X \wedge Y) \simeq F(X) \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} F(Y)$. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThese equivalences are compatible with the associativity and unitality [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconstraints (they arise from the coherent unit isomorphisms of $(Sp, \wedge, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{S})$), so $F$ is strong monoidal.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**$U$ is strong monoidal.** We must exhibit natural equivalences $U(M [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\otimes_{\mathbb{S}} N) \simeq U(M) \wedge U(N)$ and $U(\mathbb{S}) \simeq [0m
