[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{S}$ as an $\mathbb{S}$-module). ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- **Tensor product:** The relative tensor product $M \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} N$ is [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcomputed as the geometric realization of the bar construction $\text{Bar}(M, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{S}, N)$, which is the simplicial object[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$[n] \longmapsto M \wedge \mathbb{S}^{\wedge n} \wedge N.$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSince $\mathbb{S}$ is the unit of $\wedge$, we have $\mathbb{S}^{\wedge n} [0m
