[38;2;124;124;124mbuilt from the unit isomorphisms $\mathbb{S} \wedge \mathbb{S} \simeq [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{S}$ and the $\mathbb{S}$-action on $M, N$) are all equivalences. Hence [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe simplicial object is essentially constant at $M \wedge N$, and its geometric[0m[38;2;124;124;124mrealization is equivalent to $M \wedge N$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$M \otimes_{\mathbb{S}} N \simeq M \wedge N = U(M) \wedge U(N).$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m✓[0m

